    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, labelled `FY<YY>` by its ending calendar year \u2014 matching the app's Australian conventions).\n\n**New utility** \u2014 `util/FiscalYears.java`: derives the fiscal year, its two-digit segment, and the `FY<YY>` label from the (already business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`. A date in July\u2013December falls in the fiscal year ending the following calendar year (e.g. 2026-09-11 \u2192 `FY27`).\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`fiscalYear` field** \u2014 added to `openapi.yml` (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets it) and mapped in `OwnerMapper` as `FiscalYears.label(...)`. Satisfies the new `coreReturnsFiscalYear` test (`FY\\d{2}`).\n- **Membership identifier year segment** \u2014 `membershipNumber`'s `-M<YY>` now uses the fiscal-year segment instead of `registrationDate.getYear() % 100`, updated in both call sites (`OwnerMapper` and the duplicated construction in `AuditOwnerCreated`). Verified in the audit log: `NSW-16E6609E-M27`.\n- **Tenure** \u2014 `MembershipLevels` now counts elapsed 1-July fiscal years (`fiscalYear(now) \u2212 fiscalYear(registration)`) instead of 365-day windows; the 3-point bonus triggers for tenure over one fiscal year.\n- **Docs** \u2014 refreshed the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: the spec fixed the `FY<YY>` format and the 1-July start but not the labelling convention or the exact tenure threshold. I labelled fiscal years by their **ending** calendar year (standard AU convention) and set the bonus at **more than one** elapsed fiscal year, as the direct structural analog of the old \"over 365 days\" rule. No test pins exact values for these, but let me know if you intended the starting-year label or a `>= 1` threshold instead.",
